<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria M1 rises 15.7 pct, M2 up 2.54 pct in week.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria M1 rises 15.7 pct, M2 up 2.54 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply rose to 583.7 billion levs on April 11 from 504.5 billion levs a week earlier and M2 rose to 3,089.1 billion levs from 3,012.7 billion levs, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Total broad money increased 2.14 percent to 3,282.1 billion levs in the week to April 11.</p>
<p>Conversion of dollar-denominated deposits into levs was made at an exchange rate of 1,560.9 levs per dollar on April 11 against 1,599.9 on April 4.</p>
